"""
Base class for convection-coefficient models: heat flow from a surface area `A` at a
film coefficient `h`.

Ported from `ShipSIM.Components.Others.HeatTransfer.ConvectionFactors.Internal.ConvectionBaseClass`,
which is the same component as `ThermalComponents.Interfaces.ConvectiveElement1D` — same
`solid` / `fluid` heat ports, same `ΔT = solid.T - fluid.T`, same heat-flow sign
convention — plus the surface area, the film coefficient and the film temperature. This
port keeps only that difference and extends the library interface:

```math
Q_{flow} = h \\, A \\, \\Delta T
```

An extending component supplies `A` and `h`. `Tavg` is the arithmetic film temperature,
at which a correlation's fluid properties should be evaluated.

Upstream gives its four convection factors two different shapes: `ConvectionHorizontalCylinder`
and `PlateForcedConvection` extend this base class, while `InternalConvection` and
`ExternalConvection` instead wrap a `Modelica.Thermal.HeatTransfer.Components.Convection`
and drive its `Gc`, exposing `port_Solid` / `port_Fluid`. All four extend this base class
here, so every convection factor has the same ports and reports `h` and `A` the same way.
The wrapping shape remains available as `ThermalComponents.Components.Convection`, whose
`Gc` is a `RealInput`, for a coefficient computed outside the element.
"""
partial component ConvectionBaseClass
  extends ThermalComponents.Interfaces.ConvectiveElement1D
  "Heat transfer surface area [m²]"
  variable A::Area
  "Film (convective) heat transfer coefficient [W/(m²·K)]"
  variable h::CoefficientOfHeatTransfer
  "Film temperature, (solid.T + fluid.T) / 2 [K]"
  variable Tavg::Temperature
relations
  # ΔT is what the solver is left to find where a face carries no capacitance, and the
  # correlations are weakest exactly where it is small.
  guess ΔT = 0
  Tavg = (solid.T + fluid.T) / 2
  Q_flow = h * A * ΔT
end
